# The leg tag Portable (plan 5.18.10 PX4, P-1a): lit-legs.ps1 -Portable adds
# the legs tagged Portable, portable-smoke and portable-smoke-wsl, to the legs
# that a run takes, where portable-smoke-wsl (a name ending in -wsl) also
# needs -Wsl, as an Exit leg does; -List marks them 'name (-Portable)'. Each
# Portable leg first runs its setup, 'build-builtins.py --triple
# msil64-unknown-dotnet' with the build directory, through $MsilPython, and a
# failed setup is the leg's FAIL row without a lit run. Against the stand-in
# build of Inputs/ci-legs.py, whose lit passes, Inputs/legs-check.py checks:
# (1) -List and -Describe name the same legs in the same order, each listed
# with the switch of its tag, and the Portable legs are exactly the pair.
# (2) The rows (MSIL_CI_RESULTS) of a run with -Portable, with -Wsl -Portable
# and with -Exit are exactly the legs of that set: -Portable takes
# portable-smoke, -Wsl -Portable both, -Exit neither. The stand-in build has
# no bin/clang.exe, so the real build-builtins.py fails each setup (exit 2)
# and each Portable leg is a FAIL row naming its setup log; with the non-lit
# legs, which the stand-in cannot pass, each run exits 1.
# (3) With a stand-in Python (Inputs/ci-legs.py python, MSIL_PYTHON) that
# plays build-builtins.py and, from P-1b, the setup's second step
# build-libc.py (MSIL_FAKE_LIBC=ok here; describe.test checks that step):
# MSIL_FAKE_BUILTINS=ok makes -Leg portable-smoke
# and -Leg portable-smoke-wsl PASS rows whose setup ran with the build
# directory and the portable triple and whose one lit invocation passes
# exactly the paths, params and lit arguments of -Describe; =fail makes
# portable-smoke a FAIL row with exit status 1 and no lit run.
# (4) The failure path: a planted tag fails the checks it must fail:
# portable-smoke untagged the -List check; portable-smoke planted as Exit
# the -Portable run, which has it, and the -Exit run, which lacks it; and
# the -Portable rows checked without --portable.
# portable-tag-sh.test checks lit-legs.sh --portable; exit-matrix-legs.test
# checks run-m1-gate.ps1's -Portable (Get-ExpectedLegs).
# REQUIRES: msil-ci-pwsh

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py setup %t/build

